1}, {"value": "Revision History", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Compiled By Checked By Date Description V ersion", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Muhammad", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Maaz", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Sir Hamza Imran 07-Oct-2026 Long proposal structure", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and content", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "1.0", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Zain Ali Kiani Sir Hamza Imran 07-Oct-2026 Module and feature", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "review", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "1.1", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Danish Faraz Sir Hamza Imran 07-Oct-2026 Workflow and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "technology review", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "1.2", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Project Team Sir Hamza Imran 07-Oct-2026 Final 12-module draft 1.3", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 3]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "1. Project Stream", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✓ Web-Based FYP Desktop Application", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Mobile Application Game", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Hardware-Based", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "2. Introduction", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Final Year Project (FYP) management is a multi-stage academic process involving", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "proposal processing, project allocation, collaboration, project completion, evaluation,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and administrative coordination. Prior FYP-management research has shown that these", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "activities benefit from centralized digital workflows and role-specific collaboration tools", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "rather than disconnected manual processes [1, 2]. In many university environments,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "forms, spreadsheets, emails, messaging applications, and loosely organized digital records", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "can make proposal tracking, supervisor coordination, evaluation, and reuse of previous", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "project knowledge difficult.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYPHubis proposed as a centralized, role-aware, AI-assisted platform for managing", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "the complete FYP lifecycle. The platform is designed for five major roles: Student, Super-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "visor, FYP Coordinator, Panel Member, and Administrator. It combines deterministic", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "academic rules with Large Language Models (LLMs), semantic embeddings, Retrieval-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Augmented Generation (RAG), GraphRAG, machine-learning based risk analysis, opti-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "mization techniques, and agentic AI orchestration. RAG provides language models with", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "retrieved external evidence for knowledge-intensive generation, while GraphRAG extends", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "retrieval with graph-structured relationships for broader and multi-hop reasoning over", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "document collections [3, 4]. AI is used for assistance, analysis, retrieval, explanation, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "prediction, while final academic authority remains with authorized university personnel.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The FYP is organized into twelve clearly separated modules. Each module owns a", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "distinct part of the FYP lifecycle so that proposal management, quality compliance, orig-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "inality checking, supervision, scheduling, evaluation, progress monitoring, institutional", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "knowledge retrieval, and final archiving do not overlap unnecessarily.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "3. Project Description", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYPHub is a responsive web-based platform that digitizes and intelligently connects", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "the complete Final Year Project process. Students can form groups, find compatible", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "teammates, create and submit proposal versions, run AI-assisted compliance checks, com-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "pare proposals against previous FYPs, and request suitable supervisors. Supervisors can", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "review proposals using structured comments and revision requests, while the Coordina-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tor manages academic routing and panel readiness. The system also schedules defenses,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "supports structured panel evaluation, tracks project progress and supervision evidence,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "archives completed FYPs, and makes institutional project knowledge searchable through", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "RAG and GraphRAG.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The platform follows a shared-module, role-based-access architecture. A feature is not", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "duplicated into separate modules merely because different roles can view it. For example,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "the proposal compliance engine remains one module, but students, supervisors, coordina-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tors, and panel members access different views according to their permissions. Similarly,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "the final archive creates and preserves institutional knowledge, while the knowledge-search", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "module retrieves and reasons over that archived information.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The system is expected to provide a single source of truth for proposal versions,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 4]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "supervisor assignments, review comments, coordinator actions, panel evaluations, project", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "progress, and final project outcomes. This improves traceability and supports data-driven", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "academic decision making across the entire FYP lifecycle.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "4. Real World Problem", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Universities generate a large amount of valuable FYP knowledge every semester, but", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "that knowledge is often difficult to search, compare, and reuse. Students may not know", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "whether an idea has already been implemented, what limitations previous projects had,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "which supervisor is most suitable, or which university formatting and proposal require-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ments are still unmet. Group formation can also be difficult when students do not have", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "suitable teammates, and duplicate membership can occur if group rules are not centrally", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "enforced.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYP administration also involves several academic actors. Students submit propos-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "als, supervisors review them, coordinators control academic routing, panels evaluate the", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "work, and administrators configure academic rules and deadlines. When these activities", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "are distributed across disconnected tools, important context is lost. Revision comments", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "can become scattered, supervisor capacity may be unclear, panel scheduling can create", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "conflicts, progress evidence may remain informal, and completed projects can become", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "static files rather than reusable institutional knowledge.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The real-world challenge is therefore broader than simple proposal submission. The", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "university needs an integrated system that manages the workflow, applies deterministic", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "academic rules, provides AI-assisted analysis where appropriate, preserves an auditable", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "history, and converts historical FYP records into an active knowledge base for future", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "students and faculty.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "5. Problem Statement", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Current FYP management practices may suffer from fragmented team formation,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "manual proposal submission, inconsistent formatting, weak originality checks, limited", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "visibility of supervisor expertise and capacity, scattered review communication, man-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ual defense scheduling, disconnected panel feedback, limited progress evidence, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "poor reuse of completed-project knowledge. Existing generic learning-management,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "plagiarism-detection, and project-management tools can support individual parts of this", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "process, but they do not provide a unified FYP-specific platform that connects academic", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "workflow, proposal intelligence, supervisor allocation, panel evaluation, project progress,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and institutional knowledge.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The proposed project aims to develop theFYPHubplatform, which manages the", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "complete FYP lifecycle through twelve integrated but non-overlapping modules. The", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "system will combine role-based workflow control with AI-assisted proposal compliance,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "semantic originality analysis, supervisor matching, revision verification, scheduling opti-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "mization, progress and risk intelligence, RAG-based institutional knowledge search, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "final project handover support.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "6. Names of Existing Similar FYPs (if repeated)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "No exact repeated FYP has been confirmed in the current project records at proposal", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "stage. However, the problem space overlaps partially with learning-management systems,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "plagiarism/similarity platforms, project-management tools, and institutional repositories.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The proposed FYPHub differs by integrating the complete FYP lifecycle and by using", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "archived institutional FYP data as an active source for similarity analysis, knowledge", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "retrieval, extension guidance, and analytics.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 5]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The proposed system will also contain its ownProposal Similarity & Originality", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Checkmodule. Once historical FYP records are available in the repository, this module", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "will compare a new proposal against previous projects and provide evidence of semantic,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "functional, and methodological overlap rather than relying only on title similarity.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "7. New Functionalities (main) to be added Features", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYPHub introduces several capabilities that are not normally available together in a", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "single FYP management platform: ", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•AI-assisted teammate discovery using compatibility questions, skills, availability,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "work style, and role preferences, with duplicate-group membership prevention.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•University-template-aware proposal compliance checking for structure, headings,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "margins, spacing, alignment, required sections, and academic consistency.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Semantic and functional comparison of new proposals against archived FYPs, in-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "cluding contribution boundaries and extension gaps.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Expertise, workload, preference, and capacity-based supervisor recommendation", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and allocation with slot enforcement.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Structured supervisor comments, revision requests, two-way discussion, and AI-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "assisted verification of whether requested revisions were resolved.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Coordinator-controlled academic routing with delay and workflow-conformance", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "monitoring.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Conflict-aware defense scheduling and panel assignment based on availability,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "room/time constraints, and academic conflicts.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Panel scoring and feedback with AI-generated viva questions, evaluator disagree-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ment detection, and feedback-resolution tracking.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Supervision-meeting evidence, milestone tracking, project-health classification,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "delay-risk analysis, and recovery recommendations.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Final FYP archiving with implemented-scope extraction, limitations, future work,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "reusable assets, and intelligent handover packages.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•RAG/GraphRAG-based institutional FYP search with evidence and multi-hop rea-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "soning over archived projects.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Institutional analytics for domain trends, workload, turnaround time, completion", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "patterns, and management insights.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "8. Application Review", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "This section reviews six existing platforms that address selected parts of the FYP", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "lifecycle. Each application is summarized through two key characteristics and two limita-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tions, followed by a feature-by-application comparison table in the same tabular pattern", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "used throughout this proposal. The purpose is to show which capabilities already exist", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "in established systems and which FYP-specific gaps remain.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 6]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "8.1 Moodle Assignment Activity [5]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Moodle provides structured assignment submission, group submissions, deadlines,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "grading, feedback, and rubric-based assessment within a learning-management environ-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ment.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 1: Students can submit files or online text individually or in", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "groups, with configurable availability and due dates.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 2: Instructors can grade submissions, provide feedback, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "use rubrics or custom grading scales.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The limitations of Moodle for the target FYP lifecycle are listed below.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 1: It does not provide FYP-specific supervisor expertise/capacity", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "matching, allocation optimization, or defense-panel scheduling.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 2: It does not provide institutional FYP semantic originality analysis,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "GraphRAG reasoning, or intelligent handover/continuation support.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "8.2 Turnitin Similarity Report [6]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Turnitin compares submitted text against large source collections and produces a Sim-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ilarity Report that highlights matching text, source information, and an overall similarity", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "percentage.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 1: Text matching against internet sources, publications, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "previously submitted work with source-level evidence.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 2: Similarity reports support academic review by grouping", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and presenting matched passages for human interpretation.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The limitations of Turnitin for the target FYP lifecycle are listed below.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 1: It primarily measures textual similarity and does not evaluate FYP", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "problem, objectives, modules/features, methodology, implemented scope, and con-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tribution boundaries as one semantic project comparison.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 2: It does not manage FYP team formation, supervisor allocation,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "coordinator routing, defense scheduling, project-progress intelligence, or final han-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "dover.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "8.3 OpenProject [7]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "OpenProject is a general project-management and collaboration platform supporting", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "planning, tasks, milestones, workloads, timelines, and project progress.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 1: Work packages, tasks, milestones, timelines, and responsi-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "bilities can be planned and tracked across a project lifecycle.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 2: Team collaboration, workload planning, project dash-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "boards, and status tracking support coordinated project delivery.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The limitations of OpenProject for the target FYP lifecycle are listed below.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 1: It does not provide university-template proposal compliance, histor-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ical FYP originality intelligence, or formal supervisor revision-compliance checking.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 2: It does not provide FYP-specific supervisor allocation, panel evalu-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ation, institutional FYP archive reasoning, or GraphRAG-based knowledge search.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 7]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "8.4 Microsoft Teams for Education [8]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Microsoft Teams for Education combines class communication, channels, assignments,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "due dates, resources, feedback, and rubric-based grading in one collaborative environ-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ment.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 1: Channels and class-team communication support collabo-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ration among students and educators.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 2: Assignments support due dates, file submission, resubmis-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "sion, resources, grades, and rubrics.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The limitations of Microsoft Teams for Education for the target FYP lifecycle are listed", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "below.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 1: It does not provide FYP-specific teammate compatibility matching,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "supervisor expertise/capacity allocation, or historical FYP originality analysis.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 2: It does not manage coordinator academic routing, defense-panel", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "optimization, project handover intelligence, or RAG/GraphRAG reasoning over", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYP archives.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "8.5 GitHub Projects [9]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "GitHub Projects supports software-team planning and tracking through issues, pull", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "requests, project boards, tables, roadmaps, custom fields, and code-linked work items.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 1: Issues and Projects can organize tasks, ideas, bugs, mile-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "stones, and development work with configurable views and metadata.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 2: Work tracking is closely linked with repositories, pull re-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "quests, and software-development activity.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The limitations of GitHub Projects for the target FYP lifecycle are listed below.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 1: It is development-work oriented and does not provide university", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "proposal formatting/compliance, supervisor matching, or formal academic routing.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 2: It does not provide defense scheduling, panel rubric evaluation,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "semantic comparison with archived FYPs, or institutional FYP handover workflows.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "8.6 DSpace Institutional Repository [10]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "DSpace is an institutional repository platform for managing, preserving, controlling", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "access to, and searching digital content and metadata.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 1: It preserves multiple digital formats and supports", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "metadata/full-text search for institutional collections.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 2: Granular access control and repository organization sup-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "port long-term institutional knowledge preservation.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The limitations of DSpace for the target FYP lifecycle are listed below.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 1: It is primarily a repository and does not manage active FYP team", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "formation, proposal review, supervisor allocation, progress, or defense workflows.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Limitation 2: Standard repository search does not provide FYP-specific seman-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tic originality analysis, revision verification, or RAG/GraphRAG-based multi-hop", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "academic reasoning by itself.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 8]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "8.7 FYPHub (Our FYP)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYPHub combines the complete university FYP lifecycle in one role-aware platform", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "instead of treating submission, similarity checking, supervision, evaluation, progress, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "institutional knowledge as disconnected activities.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 1: Integrated 12-module workflow covering team formation,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "proposal compliance/originality, supervisor allocation/revision, coordinator control,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "defense/panel processes, project progress, final archive, and handover.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Key characteristic 2: AI-assisted institutional intelligence using LLMs, embed-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "dings, RAG/GraphRAG, optimization, and evidence-based analysis while retaining", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "human academic authority.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Table 1: Applications Comparison", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "F eature Moodle[5] T urnitin[6] OpenProject[7] MST eams[8] GitHub[9] DSpace[10] FYPHub", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Assignment/document", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "submission and deadlines", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✓ ✓ ✗ ✓ ✗ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Team collaboration and work", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tracking", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✗ ✗ ✓ ✓ ✓ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Similarity/originality", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "evidence", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✗ ✓ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Rubric-based", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "evaluation/feedback", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✓ ✓ ✗ ✓ ✗ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Institutional", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "repository/archive", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "preservation", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✓ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "University proposal", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "format/compliance analysis", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Supervisor expertise/capacity", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "allocation", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Historical FYP", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "semantic/functional", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "comparison", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Defense scheduling and panel", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "assignment", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "RAG/GraphRAG reasoning", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "over archived FYPs", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Final FYP", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "handover/continuation", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "intelligence", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✗ ✓", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "9. Scope", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The scope of FYPHub covers the complete university FYP lifecycle through twelve", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "integrated modules. The system is software-based and uses role-aware workflows, de-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "terministic academic rules, and AI-assisted analysis while preserving human academic", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "authority.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "9.1 Included Aspects", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Role-based web access for Student, Supervisor, FYP Coordinator, Panel Member,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and Administrator users.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 9]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Student team formation, proposal submission/versioning, university-format com-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "pliance, and proposal originality analysis.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Supervisor matching/allocation, supervisor-led proposal review/revision, coordina-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tor routing, defense scheduling, and panel evaluation.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Supervision evidence, milestone/progress monitoring, project-risk assistance, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "recovery recommendations.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Final FYP archiving, handover/continuation knowledge, RAG/GraphRAG search,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and institutional analytics.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "9.2 Excluded Aspects", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Automatic replacement of supervisor, coordinator, panel, or administrator academic", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "decisions by AI; authorized personnel retain final authority.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•University processes outside the FYP lifecycle such as general admissions, fee pro-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "cessing, and non-FYP academic administration.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Development of proprietary hardware or a native mobile application; the proposed", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "system is a web-based software platform.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Use of confidential institutional or student data outside approved access permissions", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and role-based policies.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "9.3 Modules Description", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 1: Admin Dashboard & Academic Management", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module provides the administrative foundation of the platform.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "It allows authorized administrators to manage users, roles, academic cycles, proposal", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "templates, supervisor capacity, evaluation rubrics, deadlines, reminders, escalation rules,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and audit history.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•User and role management for Students, Supervisors, Coordinators, Panel Members,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and Administrators.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Semester and FYP-cycle configuration including group-size and workflow policies.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Official short-proposal and long-proposal template management with versioned aca-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "demic rules.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Supervisor capacity, panel rubric, scoring criteria, and academic-deadline configu-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ration.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Deadline reminder/escalation rules and immutable audit history of administrative", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "changes.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Academic governance configuration and deadline action rules.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 2: Student Team & Collaboration Hub", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module manages student group formation and project collabo-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ration. It supports AI-assisted teammate discovery for students who do not yet have a", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "complete group and enforces the university rule that a student cannot belong to more", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "than one active FYP group in the same cycle.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 10]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•FYP group creation, leader/member rules, group-size enforcement, and verified", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "membership.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Duplicate-group membership prevention using Student ID/Registration Number", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and current FYP cycle.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•AI teammate compatibility matching using 8–10 questions covering skills, domain,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "availability, working style, preferred role, and commitment.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Join requests, invitations, accept/reject workflow, student-to-group matching, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "temporary match chat.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Seven collaboration channels (General, Proposal, Research, Supervisor Discussion,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Tasks & Progress, Files & Resources, Announcements & Deadlines) plus a group", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "AI chatbot.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Verified and compatible FYP team with a shared collaboration", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "workspace.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 3: Student Proposal & AI Compliance Check", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module owns the official proposal record and validates a student’s", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "short or long proposal against the university template and academic-quality rules. The", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "same analysis can be viewed by authorized supervisors, coordinators, and panel members", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "according to role permissions.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Short/long proposal creation, upload, draft, submit, resubmit, and lifecycle-status", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "management.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Version history with AI-generated change summaries between proposal versions.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•University-format checking for font, font size, margins, alignment, line spacing,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "heading styles, page numbering, tables, and figures.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Structural validation for required sections, section order, headings, references, ap-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "pendices, and captions.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Academic consistency analysis across problem statement, objectives, methodology,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "proposed solution, scope, and expected outcomes.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Official proposal version and Proposal Compliance & Readiness Re-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "port.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 4: Proposal Similarity & Originality Check", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module compares a new proposal with archived FYPs to deter-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "mine how much of the idea, problem, implementation scope, and methodology overlaps", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "with previous work and where a genuine contribution can begin.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Semantic embedding search against historical FYP records.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Multi-level comparison of title, problem statement, objectives, modules/features,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and methodology.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Evidence showing the most related previous projects and their implemented scope.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 11]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Contribution-boundary analysis separating inherited/overlapping work from gen-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "uinely new work.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Gap and extension analysis based on previous limitations, missing features, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "unfinished scope.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Originality, duplication, and contribution-boundary report.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 5: Supervisor Selection & Allocation", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module identifies suitable supervisors and manages the complete", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "assignment process using expertise relevance, research interests, current workload, capac-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ity, and academic constraints.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•AI-based supervisor expertise matching using proposal content, research interests,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and previous supervision history.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Ranked supervisor recommendations with explainable match reasons and expertise", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "gaps.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Supervisor capacity and slot management showing total, filled, and available slots.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Student request, supervisor accept/reject, duplicate-request protection, and final", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "assignment workflow.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Fair allocation and conflict checking using workload, preferences, capacity, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "academic constraints.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Explainable supervisor recommendation and valid final assignment.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 6: Supervisor Proposal Review Dashboard", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: After assignment, this module manages the formal supervisor-led pro-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "posal review process. Comments and requested changes remain linked to proposal versions", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "so that the academic revision history is fully traceable.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Paragraph-level, section-level, module-level, and full-proposal comments.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Editing suggestions and formal revision requests from the assigned supervisor.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Two-way student-supervisor discussion linked to the relevant proposal/revision", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "item.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Semantic comparison between old and revised proposal versions.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•AI revision-compliance checking that classifies requested changes as Resolved, Par-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tially Resolved, or Unresolved while leaving final authority with the supervisor.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Revision Resolution Report and approved/revised proposal history.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 7: Coordinator Proposal Control", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module gives the FYP Coordinator controlled academic routing", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "over supervisor-approved proposals and provides visibility into delayed, incomplete, or", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "workflow-inconsistent cases.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Dedicated queue of supervisor-approved proposals ready for coordinator action.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 12]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Hold, return-to-student, return-to-supervisor, and forward-to-panel actions.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Version-aware, immutable history of coordinator decisions and reasons.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Workflow bottleneck and abnormal-delay detection across proposal stages.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Priority and conformance monitoring for urgent cases, skipped stages, unresolved", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "requirements, and deadline risk.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Coordinator decision record and panel-ready proposal state.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 8: Panel Scheduling & Defense", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module manages defense logistics after a proposal/project be-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "comes eligible for panel evaluation. It allocates panel members, time slots, and rooms", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "while preventing scheduling and academic conflicts.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Panel-member assignment for eligible FYP groups.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Availability management for panel members, supervisors, student groups, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "rooms.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Defense date, time, room, or online-session scheduling.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Automatic detection of panel, supervisor, student, room, and conflict-of-interest", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "clashes.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Optimized scheduling and rescheduling to reduce conflicts and balance panel work-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "load.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Conflict-free defense schedule and panel assignment.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 9: Panel Evaluation & Feedback", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module manages formal panel evaluation using configured rubrics.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "It supports detailed feedback, AI-assisted defense preparation, evaluator-disagreement", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "detection, and traceable feedback resolution.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Criterion-based rubric scoring and recommendation by multiple panel members.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Paragraph, section, module/feature, and overall proposal/project comments.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•AI-generated viva/defense questions based on proposal content and claimed contri-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "bution.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Detection of significant evaluator disagreement in scores or assessment dimensions.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Feedback-resolution workflow: Panel Comment→Coordinator Resolution→Stu-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "dent/Supervisor Revision→Panel Recheck, while preserving the original panel", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "comment.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Structured panel evaluation, feedback history, and resolution status.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 10: Project Progress & Supervision Dashboard", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module combines formal supervision evidence with milestone and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "task progress to present the current health of an active FYP and identify delay or delivery", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "risks.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 13]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Supervision meeting records, minutes, decisions, action items, owners, and due", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "dates.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•AI extraction of tasks, owners, commitments, and deadlines from meeting notes.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Milestone, task, completion-percentage, overdue-work, and scope-progress tracking.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Project-health classification such as On Track, Attention Required, or Critical using", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "recorded evidence.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Risk explanation and recovery recommendations; when sufficient labelled data be-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "comes available, predictive ML models and explainability can be added for delay", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "probability estimation.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Project Progress, Action Compliance, Risk, and Recovery Report.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 11: Final FYP Archive & Handover", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module creates the final institutional record of a completed FYP", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and prepares reusable knowledge for future students instead of treating the final report", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "as a static file.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Final project submission package containing report, proposal, source-code reposi-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tory, dataset/model information, and supporting files.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Automatic extraction of project metadata including domain, technologies, datasets,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "modules, and methodology.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Classification of final scope as Completed, Partially Implemented, or Not Imple-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "mented.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Extraction of limitations, unresolved issues, technical debt, and future work.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Intelligent handover/continuation package containing reusable assets, dependencies,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "incomplete work, and recommended continuation points.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Final Project Archive Package and Continuation/Handover Package.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Module 12: FYP Knowledge Search & Analytics", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Description: This module reads and reasons over archived institutional FYP knowl-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "edge. It provides evidence-based natural-language search for authorized users and pro-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "duces institutional analytics without editing the underlying archive.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Natural-language semantic search over archived FYP titles, abstracts, modules,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "technologies, datasets, outcomes, and limitations.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•RAG and GraphRAG-based question answering grounded in retrieved institutional", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "evidence.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Multi-hop queries across relationships such as Project→Technology→Dataset→", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Limitation→Supervisor.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Source citations/evidence paths so generated answers can be traced to archived", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYP records.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 14]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Institutional analytics for domain trends, supervisor workload, approval turnaround,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "completion/delay patterns, panel statistics, and technology usage over time.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Primary Output: Evidence-Based FYP Knowledge Answers and Institutional Analyt-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ics Report.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "10. Modules", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Table 2 provides the module distribution and task allocation according to the four", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "implementation checkpoints. The same pattern is used for each checkpoint: three modules", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "are scheduled in P1 Mid, three in P1 Final, three in P2 Mid, and three in P2 Final.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Table 2: FYPHub Module Distribution and Task Allocation", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Deadline Modules Student", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "P1 Mid 1: Admin Dashboard & Academic Management Muhammad Maaz", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "(23108179)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "2: Student Team & Collaboration Hub Zain Ali Kiani", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "(23108197)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "3: Student Proposal & AI Compliance Check Danish Faraz (23108160)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "P1 Final 4: Proposal Similarity & Originality Check Muhammad Maaz", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "(23108179)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "5: Supervisor Selection & Allocation Zain Ali Kiani", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "(23108197)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "6: Supervisor Proposal Review & Revision Danish Faraz (23108160)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "P2 Mid 7: Coordinator Proposal Control Muhammad Maaz", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "(23108179)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "8: Defense & Panel Scheduling Zain Ali Kiani", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "(23108197)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "9: Panel Evaluation & Feedback Danish Faraz (23108160)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "P2 Final 10: Project Progress & Supervision Dashboard Muhammad Maaz", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "(23108179)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "11: Final FYP Archive & Handover Zain Ali Kiani", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "(23108197)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "12: FYP Knowledge Search & Analytics Danish Faraz (23108160)", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 15]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "11. Development Environment", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Tools: Visual Studio Code, Git/GitHub, PowerShell, Docker, Docker", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Compose, Swagger/OpenAPI, and Ollama for local AI model", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "execution.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "DBMS: PostgreSQL with the pgvector extension for transactional", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "academic data, proposal/version history, workflow records, archive", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "metadata, and semantic vector search.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Platform: Web-Based; Front-End: React + Vite + TypeScript with", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Tailwind CSS; Back-End: Python 3.12 with FastAPI for", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "authenticated REST APIs, academic workflow rules, and AI", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "service orchestration.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "AI Envi-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ronment: ", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Local and/or approved language models through Ollama,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "embedding models, RAG/GraphRAG pipelines, Python-based AI", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "orchestration, machine-learning libraries for risk analysis, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "optimization libraries for scheduling/allocation.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "12. Significance", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYPHub is significant because it transforms the university’s FYP process from a", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "collection of disconnected administrative tasks into a connected academic intelligence", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ecosystem. The platform does not only digitize proposal forms; it links team formation,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "proposal quality, originality, supervision, coordinator routing, scheduling, panel evalua-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "tion, progress evidence, final archiving, and institutional knowledge reuse.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "The main expected benefits are: ", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Improved Proposal Quality: Students receive structured feedback on university", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "formatting, missing sections, academic consistency, and readiness before formal", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "review.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Reduced Duplication: Semantic and functional comparison against previous", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYPs reveals overlap and clarifies where genuine new contribution should begin.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Better Team Formation: AI teammate matching and duplicate-membership", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "rules support fair and compatible group creation.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Transparent Supervision: Supervisor selection considers expertise and capacity,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "while revision comments and meeting actions remain traceable.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Efficient Academic Routing: Coordinators can monitor proposal states, delays,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and panel readiness from one controlled workflow.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Improved Defense Management: Panel assignments and defense schedules are", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "generated with conflict and availability checks.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Evidence-Based Progress Monitoring: Meeting actions, milestones, tasks, and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "delays contribute to project-health and recovery recommendations.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Institutional Knowledge Reuse: Final FYPs become searchable, reusable", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "knowledge through RAG/GraphRAG and analytics rather than remaining isolated", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "documents.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 16]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Human-Controlled AI: AI supports analysis, explanation, retrieval, prediction,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "and recommendations, while authorized academic personnel retain final decision", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "authority.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "13. Tools and Techniques", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYPHub uses a modular web and AI architecture that separates deterministic aca-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "demic rules from probabilistic AI assistance. The major tools and techniques are listed", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "below.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Front-End: React + Vite + TypeScript with Tailwind CSS will provide responsive", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "role-specific interfaces for Student, Supervisor, Coordinator, Panel, and Adminis-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "trator users [11].", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Back-End: Python 3.12 with FastAPI will provide authenticated REST APIs, role-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "based authorization, academic workflow rules, AI-service endpoints, and integration", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "logic [12].", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Database: PostgreSQL will store users, teams, proposals, versions, assignments,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "reviews, coordinator actions, schedules, evaluations, progress records, and archive", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "metadata [13]. The pgvector extension will support proposal embeddings, semantic", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "retrieval, and historical FYP similarity search [14].", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•AI and Intelligence: LLMs and embeddings will support proposal-quality anal-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ysis, semantic revision checking, teammate explanations, viva-question generation,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "summarization, and semantic search. RAG will ground generated answers in re-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "trieved institutional evidence [3], while GraphRAG will add graph-structured re-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "trieval for broader and multi-hop reasoning across archived FYP relationships [4].", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Optimization techniques will support supervisor allocation and defense scheduling,", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "while project-risk analysis will begin with deterministic/hybrid evidence and may", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "later use supervised ML when sufficient labelled data becomes available.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Security and Academic Rules: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) and de-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "terministic backend/database constraints will enforce group uniqueness, supervisor", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "slots, proposal-version eligibility, coordinator routing, panel permissions, and ad-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ministrative policies rather than delegating these controls to an LLM.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "•Development Tools: Docker and Docker Compose will support reproducible", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "infrastructure [15]; Git/GitHub will support collaborative version control; Swag-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "ger/OpenAPI will support API documentation and testing; Ollama will support", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "local AI model execution.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Overall Workflow: Admin Setup→Team Formation→Proposal Submission &", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "AI Compliance→Similarity & Originality Check→Supervisor Selection & Allocation", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "→Supervisor Review & Revision→Coordinator Proposal Control→Defense & Panel", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Scheduling→Panel Evaluation & Feedback→Project Progress & Supervision→Final", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "FYP Archive & Handover→FYP Knowledge Search & Analytics.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[PAGE 17]", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "References", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[1] R. Lounas, I. Hamzaoui, N. Bouguelmouna, and H. Mokrani, “An E-Collaboration", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Application for Final-Year Project Management,”International Journal of e-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Collaboration, vol. 19, no. 1, pp. 1–17, 2023. DOI: 10.4018/IJeC.315787.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[2] A. S. Yusuf, “A Web-Based System for Final Year Student Project Allocation and", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Management,”Journal of Basics and Applied Sciences Research, vol. 4, no. 3, pp.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "9–22, 2026. DOI: 10.4314/jobasr.v4i3.2.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[3] P. Lewis et al., “Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Knowledge-Intensive NLP", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Tasks,”Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2020. Avail-", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "able: https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.11401.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "[4] D. Edge et al., “From Local to Global: A Graph RAG Approach to Query-Focused", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "Summarization,” 2024. Available: https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16130.", "source": "page 1", "source_page": 1}, {"value": "