396	508	1	student_one_page_proposal.pdf	application/pdf	44885	578da3a4b1f1c01d459972e03a92ab2aadd851743cd89364225870c38f6addda	1	\\	FYPHub: Intelligent Final Year Project Workspace\nOne-Page Student Proposal\n1. Problem Statement\nStudents and supervisors often manage proposals, feedback, documents, and previous-project references\nacross disconnected tools. This makes it difficult to verify university requirements, track decisions, and identify\nwhether a proposed idea has already been explored.\n2. Proposed Solution\nFYPHub is a role-based web workspace that centralizes student teams, supervisor requests, proposal\ndocuments, feedback, compliance checks, and an authorized archive of previous projects. It gives each\nstakeholder a clear and secure view of the work relevant to them.\n3. Objectives\n01\nCentralize project proposals, documents, conversations, and decisions.\n02\nAllow students to submit a one-page proposal PDF and request a supervisor.\n03\nHelp supervisors review proposals, provide feedback, and record decisions.\n04\nCompare proposal titles with authorized archived project references.\n4. Methodology\nThe system uses authenticated role-based access. A student uploads a one-page PDF; the platform extracts the\ntitle and purpose, shows a confirmation preview, checks relevant archived references, and submits the request\nto the selected supervisor. The supervisor can accept, reject, or request changes with feedback. All important\nactions are recorded in an auditable history.\n5. Expected Outcomes\nA transparent FYP workflow with fewer manual handoffs, faster proposal review, traceable feedback, safer\ndocument access, and better awareness of previous institutional projects.\nKeywords: FYP management, proposal review, supervisor allocation, document extraction, academic workflow, project archive	{"title": {"value": null, "source": null, "display": "Not detected in PDF", "source_page": null}, "topic": {"value": null, "source": null, "display": "Not dete